# A program pinned to JS that imports a Core module turns on the web
# partition's checks, which check every Core body. When Core was read from
# its record outside the tree, those checks met modules whose bodies were
# never checked, and the effect pass stopped indexing a one-row list by a
# Core module's position. Every compile now checks Core from source, and the
# program checks clean, on many threads and on one.
fixture: JSPinnedEntryWithACoreImportChecks.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
env: JET_STORE_DIR={work}/cache
env: JETPACK_ROOT={work}/jetpack
step: jet check main.jet
exit: 0
stderr: !~ "panic" # the check runs to the end, with no compiler stop
step: jet check --threads 1 main.jet
exit: 0
stderr: !~ "panic" # on one thread the effect pass takes its serial path, which stopped too
